"a\":\"$@12\",\"rootVaryParams\":null,\"needsRuntimeRequest\":\"$@13\"}\n25:I[38437,[\"99489\",\"static/chunks/99489-7b4b74c1a59849db.js\",\"5772\",\"static/chunks/5772-2ad3d6bb0136fa62.js\",\"57304\",\"static/chunks/57304-ca98254065b92130.js\",\"95953\",\"static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-a38ec015cb873e3f.js\"],\"Image\"]\n2a:I[90484,[],\"OutletBoundary\"]\n2b:\"$Sreact.suspense\"\n2d:I[90484,[],\"ViewportBoundary\"]\n2e:I[90484,[],\"MetadataBoundary\"]\n2f:I[86869,[],\"IconMark\"]\n30:I[57121,[],\"\"]\n31:I[74581,[],\"\"]\n5:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sticky top-28 border-t border-[var(--primary)] pt-4 font-mono text-[9px] uppercase leading-5 tracking-[0.15em] text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":[\"DigiRobotics\",[\"$\",\"br\",null,{}],\"Field note\",[\"$\",\"br\",null,{}],\"2026.11.20\"]}]\n14:T46f,The workflow that produced those 30,000 hours is structured around five design decisions that separate trainable data from raw footage. Forehead-mounted capture at a 45° downward angle, using leading consumer smartphones secured in wearable rigs, is a geometry chosen to keep hands, objects, and workspace simultaneously in frame without the bulk of dedicated hardware. Authentic activity rather than staged movements — contributors perform real tasks in real environments — household, industrial, retail, hospitality, agricultural, construction, and service settings — across multiple countries and continents. Mobile-application-driven submission with automated formatting, integrity checks, and location verification built in, removing the friction that historically capped contributor throughput. A one-day review cycle with explicit rejection reasons, enabling rapid recapture rather than waiting weeks to discover a capture error. Quality intervention is continuous rather than post-hoc. And up to 100 approved hours per participant, with each contributor generating dozens of micro-submissions over the project lifecycle.6:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-0\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"blockquote\",\"blockquote-0\",{\"className\":\"my-10 border-l-2 border-[var(--primary)] bg-[var(--primary)]/[0.06] px-6 py-2 font-heading text-xl leading-8 text-white sm:px-8\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"TL;DR:\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"Every robot policy is taught by human demonstrators whose first-person footage has historically been invisible, unpaid, or scraped without consent. A new economic category is emerging — the contributor economy for Physical AI — where everyday humans capture real tasks and get paid instantly when their footage is consumed. Production-scale capture requires an 80% yield workflow: forehead-mounted smartphone capture, authentic real environments, mobile submission, one-day QA, and up to 100 hours per participant. Autonomous stablecoin settlement makes contributor payouts economically viable at micro-payout volumes — sub-second finality, sub-cent fees, programmable governance. DigiRobotics composes both stacks into a closed loop where contributors earn USDG the moment their data is consumed.\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\",\"children\":\"Behind Every Robot Policy Is a Human Demonstrator\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"Behind every robot policy that grasps an object, navigates a kitchen, or assembles a part, there is a human demonstrator whose first-person footage taught the model what the task looks like from the inside. That demonstrator has historically been invisible — an unpaid research subject, a paid lab contractor, or a scraped video on the internet with no consent attached. A new economic category is now emerging around them: the contributor economy for Physical AI, in which everyday humans capture first-person physical tasks on accessible hardware, submit them through production-grade workflows, and get paid instantly the moment their footage is consumed by an AI agent or robotics lab. Two infrastructure layers make this possible — a production-scale capture and QA pipeline on the data side, and an autonomous stablecoin settlement stack on the payment side. Neither works alone.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\",\"children\":\"The Production-Scale Capture Workflow\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"A recent large-scale egocentric data collection program produced 30,000 hours of raw first-person video, of which only 24,000+ hours cleared annotation and quality review for model training. That 80% yield rate is the hidden tax on production-scale capture — 6,000 hours lost to framing errors, idle footage, occlusion, and quality regressions. The economics of recapture, of contributor retention, and of dataset growth all depend on closing that gap.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"$14\"}],\"\\n\",\"$L15\",\"\\n\",\"$L16\",\"\\n\",\"$L17\",\"\\n\",\"$L18\",\"\\n\",\"$L19\",\"\\n\",\"$L1a\",\"\\n\",\"$L1b\",\"\\n\",\"$L1c\",\"\\n\",\"$L1d\",\"\\n\",\"$L1e\",\"\\n\",\"$L1f\",\"\\n\",\"$L20\",\"\\n\",\"$L21\",\"\\n\",\"$L22\",\"\\n\",\"$L23\"],\"$L24\"]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"border-t border-white/[.08] bg-[#111620] py-12\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto w-full max-w-[1440px] px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-12 xl:px-16\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] lg:items-start\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L25\",null,{\"src\":\"/digirobotics/brand/digirobotics-logo.png\",\"alt\":\"DigiRobotics.xyz\",\"width\":210,\"height\":48,\"className\":\"h-auto w-[190px]\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-4 text-[17px] text-white/60\",\"children\":\"Egocentric data for robotics training.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Footer navigation\",\"className\":\"flex max-w-2xl flex-wrap gap-x-7 gap-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",\"Contributor\",{\"href\":\"/#contributors\",\"className\":\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\",\"children\":\"Contributor\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"Marketplace\",{\"href\":\"/#marketplace\",\"className\":\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\",\"children\":\"Marketplace\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"Custom Data\",{\"href\":\"/#custom-data\",\"className\":\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\",\"children\":\"Custom Data\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"Capture Gear\",{\"href\":\"/gear\",\"className\":\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\",\"children\":\"Capture Gear\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"Articles\",{\"href\":\"/blog\",\"className\":\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\",\"children\":\"Articles\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"Agent Demo\",{\"href\":\"/agent-demo\",\"className\":\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\",\"children\":\"Agent Demo\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"Privacy & Terms\",{\"href\":\"/#privacy-note\",\"className\":\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\",\"children\":\"Privacy & Terms\"}],\"$L26\"]}]]}],\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\"]}]}]\n8:[\"$\",\"$L2a\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$2b\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@2c\"}]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L2d\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2e\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$2b\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"The Contributor Economy Behind Embodied AI — DigiRobotics\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Production-scale first-person data collection and autonomous stablecoin settlement are creating a new economic category — paid human contribution to Physical AI training at planetary scale, where everyday humans earn instantly when their footage trains robot policies.\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{\"rel\":\"manifest\",\"href\":\"/manifest.webmanifest\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"3\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://digirobotics.xyz/blog/the-contributor-economy-behind-embodied-ai\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"The Contributor Economy Behind Embodied AI\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"Production-scale first-person data collection and autonomous stablecoin settlement are creating a new economic category — paid human contribution to Physical AI training at planetary scale, where everyday humans earn instantly when their footage trains robot policies.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"property\":\"og:url\",\"content\":\"https://digirobotics.xyz/blog/the-contributor-economy-behind-embodied-ai\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"property\":\"og:image\",\"content\":\"https://digirobotics.xyz/images/blog/the-contributor-economy-behind-embodied-ai-cover.jpg\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"property\":\"og:image:alt\",\"content\":\"The Contributor Economy Behind Embodied AI\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"property\":\"og:type\",\"content\":\"article\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"10\",{\"property\":\"article:published_time\",\"content\":\"2026-11-20\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"11\",{\"property\":\"article:modified_time\",\"content\":\"2026-11-20\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"12\",{\"property\":\"article:author\",\"content\":\"DigiRobotics Team\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"13\",{\"name\":\"twitter:card\",\"content\":\"summary_large_image\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"14\",{\"name\":\"twitter:title\",\"content\":\"The Contributor Economy Behind Embodied AI\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"15\",{\"name\":\"twitter:description\",\"content\":\"Production-scale first-person data collection and autonomous stablecoin settlement are creating a new economic category — paid human contribution to Physical AI training at planetary scale, where everyday humans earn instantly when their footage trains robot policies.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"16\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image\",\"content\":\"https://digirobotics.xyz/images/blog/the-contributor-economy-behind-embodied-ai-cover.jpg\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"17\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon.ico?63d5b2ef705d808e\",\"type\":\"image/x-icon\",\"sizes\":\"256x256\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"18\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/icon.png?1f3d5ce59ec9c445\",\"type\":\"image/png\",\"sizes\":\"1254x1254\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"19\",{\"rel\":\"apple-touch-icon\",\"href\":\"/apple-icon.png?1f3d5ce59ec9c445\",\"type\":\"image/png\",\"sizes\":\"1254x1254\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2f\",\"20\",{}]]}]}]}],null]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L30\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L31\",null,{}]}]]}]\n10:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L30\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L31\",null,{}]}]]}]\n13:true\n15:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"The output is explicitly designed to be robotics-ready — usable for activity recognition, hand-object interaction modeling, and robotic perception without rework. But robotics-ready data is only half the equation. The other half is paying the contributors whose footage makes it possible.\"}]\n16:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\",\"children\":\"The Settlement Stack That Pays Contributors\"}]\n32:T44f,The agentic payment stack now being standardized across the financial industry is what makes paying hundreds of distributed contributors economically viable at the transaction values involved. The stack is structured as five layers. The settlement layer uses high-throughput blockchains where stablecoin transfers reach deterministic finality in sub-seconds. The token layer uses USD-pegged stablecoins providing programmable medium of exchange with 24/7 operation and sub-cent fees. The protocol layer includes open standards including an HTTP-native agentic payment protocol — co-developed by a major cryptocurrency exchange and a leading web infrastructure provider — that has already processed over 100 million payments and reached roughly $600 million in annualized volume; an agent payments protocol backed by a coalition of more than 60 banks and tech firms; and a universal commerce protocol for merchant discovery. The application layer includes AI agents, marketplaces, and procurement workflows. And the identity and authorization layer uses verifiable credentials and mandate frameworks.17:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"$32\"}]\n18:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"The defining security principle, articulated across recent industry research, is blunt: an agent should never be the last line of defense against its own failures. The stack enforces this through a five-dimension policy engine that wraps every transaction. Spending limits are hard caps per transaction, per day, per counterparty. Counterparty allowlists mean agents can only transact with pre-approved entities. Transaction type restrictions set limits by category or merchant type. Time-based controls are windows of permitted activity. And escalation thresholds provide automatic handoff to a human when risk exceeds a defined level.\"}]\n19:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"For a contributor economy, this governance is the difference between a workable marketplace and a runaway liability. Every contributor payout flows through the policy engine before settlement, ensuring that spending caps, counterparty verification, and audit trails are enforced programmatically rather than relying on manual review.\"}]\n1a:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\",\"children\":\"The Contributor Economy Emerges\"}]\n1b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"The two stacks compose into a new economic pattern that neither enables alone.\"}]\n1c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"Consider the unit economics of a single contributor producing 100 approved hours over a project lifecycle. At a fair per-hour rate, that contributor generates dozens of micro-payouts — each one triggered by a quality review pass, a marketplace procurement event, or an autonomous agent's API call. A traditional procurement flow — invoice, approval, batch payment, 30-day settlement — collapses under the weight of that volume. The marginal cost of paying one contributor for one hour of approved footage approaches zero only if the settlement rail itself costs near zero and settles instantly.\"}]\n1d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"That is exactly what the agentic payment stack provides. The same HTTP-native payment protocol that processes API micropayments for AI agents can settle contributor payouts for egocentric data — atomically, programmatically, and without human review of each transaction. The same stablecoin settlement that delivers sub-second finality for autonomous agents can pay a contributor the moment their footage passes quality review, with no correspondent banking delays and no FX friction. The same five-dimension policy engine that prevents runaway agent spending enforces the spending caps and counterparty verification that a contributor marketplace requires.\"}]\n1e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"The reverse dependency is just as strong. Agentic commerce needs real-world tasks to settle around. The richest, most under-monetized category of real-world task data is first-person human activity — the manipulation, locomotion, and tool use that robotics labs are desperate to acquire. Without a marketplace that connects contributors to consumers programmatically, the long tail of physical-world expertise stays locked inside a handful of well-capitalized labs. Without the data that marketplace would surface, embodied AI policies plateau well below their documented scaling-law potential.\"}]\n1f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"The closed loop is clear: contributor captures first-person footage → mobile application submits and verifies → one-day QA cycle approves or rejects with explicit reasons → approved footage is tokenized and listed → autonomous agent discovers it and settles via an HTTP-native payment protocol in seconds → five-dimension policy engine enforces governance → contributor receives stablecoin payout → improved data trains improved policies → more deployment creates more demand for data → contributor captures more footage.\"}]\n20:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-4\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 mt-6 scroll-mt-24 font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-white\",\"children\":\"Conclusion\"}]\n21:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-12\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"DigiRobotics is the world's first stablecoin-native marketplace for agentic commerce in real-world robotics data — purpose-built to operationalize the contributor economy at planetary scale. Contributors capture egocentric footage of physical tasks using accessible wearable devices and smartphones, extending the production-scale capture workflow beyond any single program's cohort. Mobile-application-driven submission, multi-stage QA, and automatic anonymization preserve the yield rate that production-scale training requires.\"}]\n22:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-13\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"Settlement runs over an HTTP-native agentic payment protocol in USDG stablecoins on a high-performance Layer-2 network, with a cross-cutting five-dimension policy engine governing spending limits, counterparty allowlists, transaction type restrictions, time-based controls, and escalation thresholds for every transaction. Contributors are paid the instant their data is consumed — no invoices, no batch payouts, no 30-day settlement windows.\"}]\n23:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-14\",{\"className\":\"my-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\",\"children\":\"By composing the production-scale capture pipeline directly with the autonomous settlement stack, DigiRobotics turns the contributor economy from an aspiration into infrastructure. Everyday users earn USDG for first-person capture; autonomous agents purchase that data around the clock; Physical AI policies scale toward their documented potential. The humans who train robots finally get paid like the infrastructure they always were.\"}]\n24:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-16 border-t border-white/10 pt-8\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog\",\"className\":\"inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-white/15 px-5 py-3 text-[14px] font-semibold transition hover:border-[var(--primary)] hover:text-[var(--primary)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"icon\":\"$0:data:0:rsc:props:children:0:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:children:0:props:icon\",\"size\":16,\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],\" Return to the archive\"]}]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"a\",\"Contact Us\",{\"href\":\"mailto:hello@digirobotics.xyz\",\"className\":\"min-h-11 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white/65 relative transition-colors duration-300 ease-out after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:bottom-1 after:h-px after:origin-left after:scale-x-0 after:bg-[var(--primary)] after:transition-transform after:duration-300 after:ease-out hover:text-[var(--primary)] hover:after:scale-x-100\",\"children\":\"Contact Us\"}]\n27:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"id\":\"privacy-note\",\"className\":\"mt-10 grid gap-4 border-t border-white/[.08] pt-6 text-[13px] leading-5 text-white/45 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_auto]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Privacy and terms notices will be published before campaign enrollment or data collection begins. Contact the team for Phase 1 information.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"© 2026 DigiRobotics\"}]]}]\n28:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 flex items-center gap-4 text-white/45\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-white/45 hover:text-white transition-colors\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"icon\":{\"name\":\"x\",\"size\":24,\"node\":[[\"path\",{\"d\":\"M18 6 6 18\",\"key\":\"1bl5f8\"}],[\"path\",{\"d\":\"m6 6 12 12\",\"key\":\"d8bk6v\"}]]},\"size\":18,\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-white/45 hover:text-white transition-colors\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"icon\":{\"name\":\"mail\",\"size\":24,\"node\":[[\"path\",{\"d\":\"m22 7-8.991 5.727a2 2 0 0 1-2.009 0L2 7\",\"key\":\"132q7q\"}],[\"rect\",{\"x\":\"2\",\"y\":\"4\",\"width\":\"20\",\"height\":\"16\",\"rx\":\"2\",\"key\":\"izxlao\"}]]},\"size\":18,\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}]}]]}]\n29:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[.12em] text-white/35\",\"children\":\"Agent-compatible payment workflows powered by stablecoins and x402. Phase 1 infrastructure.\"}]\n2c:null\na:300\na:C\n12:0\nc:\"$undefined\"\ne:\"$undefined\"\n11:\"$undefined\"\n9:\"$undefined\"\n"}}